WEBVTT

00:00:01.502 --> 00:00:04.296
Prepare for
the stereophonic experience.

00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:14.306
Oh, New New York City!

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.978
Don't worry about it.

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:24.983
Do the Robot, baby!

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:44.586
Oh, Lord, hiking is always
such a strain on the buttocks.

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:48.799
Shh. What was that sound?

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.759
It wasn't a bird's nest falling.

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:52.219
That sounds like this.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:57.432
Aw, they're so cute when they're scared.

00:00:57.516 --> 00:00:59.101
I meant the sound Bigfoot just made.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:01.186
He's been sighted a lot
in this area recently.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.647
Just last week, a blind hiker felt him.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.400
Don't tell me you
actually believe in Bigfoot,

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:08.235
you blathering ninnyhammer.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.486
Of course I do.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.988
Bigfoot's my hero.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.782
Growing up, he was the celebrity
I most identified with.

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:14.867
Why?

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.994
'Cause he was a loner
who hated the popular monsters,

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.203
yet longed to be one.

00:01:18.287 --> 00:01:21.206
I can so relate to that.

00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:25.669
Ugh, enough emotions.

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:27.880
This isn't a fat camp, for God's sake.

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:29.798
Although you wouldn't know it
from looking.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.562
Bender, if you want to sleep
in a tent tonight,

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:48.192
you're welcome to join me and Hermes
for a little "just friends" spooning.

00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:50.861
Nah, I'm comfy out here under the stars.

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:52.362
Whoa! Whoa!

00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:54.656
Real comfy.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:59.536
Hi. I'm Ranger Park, the park ranger.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.621
I get it.

00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:02.789
Now, since this area's
a national Bigfoot preserve,

00:02:02.873 --> 00:02:04.666
we'll start with a short film
about Bigfoot

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.210
while I make a few phone calls.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:16.303
In the dense forests
of the Pacific Northwest

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:20.307
dwells the strange and beautiful creature
known as Bigfoot, perhaps.

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:21.808
That proves it.

00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:24.394
Sadly, logging and human settlement

00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:27.147
today threaten what might
possibly be his habitat,

00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:28.857
although if it's not, they don't.

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:33.111
Bigfoot populations require
vast amounts of land

00:02:33.195 --> 00:02:34.530
to remain elusive in.

00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:36.949
They typically dwell just behind rocks,

00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:38.617
but are also sometimes playful,

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.120
bounding into thick fogs
and out-of-focus areas.

00:02:42.538 --> 00:02:45.624
It should say "top quality
exercycle for sale."

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:47.584
And could you put "top quality" in bold?

00:02:47.668 --> 00:02:50.003
You can't? Okay, whatever.

00:02:50.254 --> 00:02:52.130
Remember, it's up to us.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:55.843
Bigfoot is a crucial part
of the ecosystem, if he exists.

00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:59.012
So, let's all help
keep Bigfoot possibly alive

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:02.266
for future generations to enjoy,
unless he doesn't exist.

00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:07.938
All right, I got to call you back.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.314
All right, questions?

00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:12.067
Yeah. Have youse ever seens Bigfeet?

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.485
Technically, no.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:16.238
But I do see him each night in my dreams

00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:19.491
and each day in the smiling
faces of hairy children.

00:03:19.575 --> 00:03:21.535
Bunk! Bunk, I say.

00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:24.997
Bring me a bag full of Bigfoot's
droppings or shut up!

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.874
I have the droppings
of someone who saw Bigfoot.

00:03:26.957 --> 00:03:28.000
Shut up!

00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:29.751
Oh, my God. Look, it's Bigfoot!

00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:30.878
Where?

00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:32.171
Ah, he's gone.

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:34.256
He said you should keep
wasting your life, though.

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:38.051
Oh, I saw Bigfoot crushing cars
at the county fair.

00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:40.929
What you saw was Bigfoot
the monster truck.

00:03:41.013 --> 00:03:42.639
But thanks for a great question.

00:03:42.723 --> 00:03:44.433
Oh...

00:03:44.516 --> 00:03:45.809
Sir, if I may?

00:03:45.893 --> 00:03:48.103
Why don't you just set up,
like, a billion video cameras

00:03:48.187 --> 00:03:50.189
in the woods and see if he walks by one.

00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:52.983
Ah, that would be very expensive,

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.611
and most people who believe
in Bigfoot are broke.

00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:57.779
Hey, look, Bigfoot, he's back!

00:03:57.863 --> 00:03:58.989
Where?

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.157
Up your face.

00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:03.410
Everybody do the Bender.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.250
The sky out here is amazing.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.085
Look at all the satellites.

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:21.762
Good night, employees.

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:23.180
Good night.

00:04:23.514 --> 00:04:25.307
Good night, Hubert.

00:04:28.352 --> 00:04:30.062
You doing all right out there, buddy?

00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:31.688
Better than these gnats.

00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:37.819
That guy won't be going home to his kids.

00:04:46.745 --> 00:04:48.080
What's that? A wolf?

00:04:48.163 --> 00:04:49.831
Or some kind of boogen?

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:52.209
Oh, God, I wish I was safe inside a tent.

00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:55.921
Fry! Fry, wake up.

00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:57.422
It's me, Bigface.

00:04:57.506 --> 00:04:59.716
Come out and groom my mangy fur.

00:05:00.884 --> 00:05:02.970
Bigfoot? You taught yourself English?

00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:06.181
Bigfoot?

00:05:06.265 --> 00:05:07.558
Bigfoot?

00:05:20.946 --> 00:05:22.865
Bigfoot, is that you?

00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:24.616
I'm not like the others, Bigfoot.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.579
I see through your monster coating
to the gentle loner inside.

00:05:28.662 --> 00:05:30.455
I bet you have a wounded raccoon friend

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:32.875
