00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.133
Well, why don't you think back

00:15:25.217 --> 00:15:27.177
to what brought you together
in the first place.

00:15:27.261 --> 00:15:29.638
Oh, I don't know.

00:15:29.721 --> 00:15:31.849
Lrrr used to be so tender.

00:15:31.932 --> 00:15:35.477
Oh, I only wrote that poem
to test my printer.

00:15:35.561 --> 00:15:37.604
We'd go walking in the woods

00:15:37.688 --> 00:15:40.023
and Lrrr would find
injured little tinklebunnies

00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:41.567
and nurse them back to health.

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.777
Yes, but I'm the one who injured them.

00:15:43.861 --> 00:15:45.028
Oh, shush.

00:15:45.112 --> 00:15:48.365
You stepped on them by accident
and then you cried all night.

00:15:48.448 --> 00:15:51.451
That's the kind of sensitive man
you used to be.

00:15:51.535 --> 00:15:55.497
And you used to wear a size three cape,
but not anymore!

00:15:55.581 --> 00:15:58.333
Now bring me that lower horn
while I'm still in the mood.

00:16:00.711 --> 00:16:03.005
But what if we
helped you get your passion back

00:16:03.088 --> 00:16:04.548
without the hassle of mutilating me?

00:16:04.631 --> 00:16:06.842
Yeah. We know a great place
in the mountains.

00:16:06.925 --> 00:16:10.095
We could take you there
for a romantic dinner under the stars.

00:16:10.179 --> 00:16:12.639
Hmm. Sounds interesting.

00:16:12.723 --> 00:16:14.099
But he would never do it.

00:16:14.183 --> 00:16:15.392
Oh, like hell I wouldn't.

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:17.561
I'm not going to be blamed for not going.

00:16:17.644 --> 00:16:19.771
Then it's a deal. We get one night.

00:16:19.855 --> 00:16:23.567
I keep my horn as long as you two
end up doing the horizontal Monster Mash.

00:16:25.903 --> 00:16:28.363
Oh... I don't get it.

00:16:34.077 --> 00:16:38.373
Bonjour. May I offer you a box of wine
for the edge of the table?

00:16:38.457 --> 00:16:40.959
No, thanks. Just water, please.

00:16:41.043 --> 00:16:42.252
Tap water.

00:16:42.336 --> 00:16:43.962
Oh, big spender.

00:16:44.046 --> 00:16:46.590
That's it! This date is over!

00:16:46.673 --> 00:16:47.841
Waiter!

00:16:49.301 --> 00:16:51.011
So, what can I get you this evening?

00:16:51.094 --> 00:16:52.471
Your lower horn!

00:16:53.764 --> 00:16:55.557
Uh, I'll just start you off
with some bread,

00:16:55.641 --> 00:16:57.726
some sexy, arousing bread.

00:16:57.809 --> 00:17:00.479
Fine, but none of that
whole-grain goat food.

00:17:00.562 --> 00:17:02.523
And bring plenty of melted butter!

00:17:02.606 --> 00:17:07.027
Ugh. Why don't you just inject
some fat straight into your ass

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.529
and cut out the middleman?

00:17:08.612 --> 00:17:12.157
One of these days, Ndnd... Bang! Zoom!

00:17:12.241 --> 00:17:14.993
Straight to the third moon
of Omicron Persei 8!

00:17:21.667 --> 00:17:24.378
Mm. This jerked chicken is good.

00:17:24.461 --> 00:17:27.005
I think I'll have Fry's lower horn jerked.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:30.092
It's used to it! Whoo!

00:17:31.593 --> 00:17:34.137
So, uh, how are you two
snoogie-pookums doing?

00:17:34.221 --> 00:17:35.264
Poorly!

00:17:35.347 --> 00:17:37.140
My wife is right, for once.

00:17:37.224 --> 00:17:39.685
There's very little magic in the air.

00:17:39.768 --> 00:17:41.979
Ready the lower horn transport vessel.

00:17:46.275 --> 00:17:49.444
Boy, who knew a cooler
could also make a handy wang coffin.

00:17:50.195 --> 00:17:52.155
Mind if I stick these in here?

00:17:52.239 --> 00:17:53.490
Go for it.

00:17:54.658 --> 00:17:55.701
Don't worry, Fry.

00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:58.871
Things look bad,
but I still have a trump card...

00:17:59.162 --> 00:18:01.707
The most beautiful love song ever written.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:09.965
And I will always love you, ooh...

00:18:14.678 --> 00:18:16.346
The humans are attacking!

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:19.183
Pluck the lower horn
and let's get out of here!

00:18:20.767 --> 00:18:22.477
Quick, Fry, run for it.

00:18:27.191 --> 00:18:29.818
Come on, freedom cage, roll me to safety.

00:18:31.862 --> 00:18:33.197
Ow, ow, ow.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.036
Yes! I never thought
I'd escape with my doodle

00:18:39.119 --> 00:18:40.829
but I pulled it out.

00:18:40.913 --> 00:18:44.333
Just like
at the movie theater. Whoo!

00:18:44.416 --> 00:18:45.501
Give me that.

00:19:06.605 --> 00:19:09.149
Bigfoot! He's real. I knew it!

00:19:09.233 --> 00:19:11.443
The Loch Ness monster's book was right.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:21.828
Well, hello there, my furry friend.

00:19:21.912 --> 00:19:24.706
Look at his adorable little feet.

00:19:33.966 --> 00:19:36.718
Yes, you are a cutie pie.

00:19:36.802 --> 00:19:38.428
Holy macaroni!

00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:42.808
I can't believe I'm seeing Bigfoot.

00:19:42.891 --> 00:19:44.268
And he's in focus.

00:19:44.351 --> 00:19:46.645
Oh, I've waited my entire life
for this moment.

00:19:49.022 --> 00:19:50.232
Huh? What?

00:19:50.315 --> 00:19:51.525
Hey, what are you doing with that?

00:19:51.608 --> 00:19:54.653
You're going to kill
this innocent giganto?

00:19:54.736 --> 00:19:56.530
Of course not.

00:19:56.613 --> 00:19:58.115
I'm just going to tranquilize him

00:19:58.198 --> 00:20:00.784
so I can chop off his feet
as proof he exists,

00:20:00.868 --> 00:20:02.578
then dump him back in the wild.

00:20:02.661 --> 00:20:03.829
He'll do fine.

00:20:04.413 --> 00:20:07.165
You'll have to get through me first.

00:20:07.249 --> 00:20:08.959
Okay. Nightie-night.

00:20:12.337 --> 00:20:13.338
Ah...

00:20:13.422 --> 00:20:17.301
Now leave this gentle Sasquatch,
or wood ape, in peace,

00:20:17.384 --> 00:20:19.386
so I can finally, and at long last,

00:20:19.469 --> 00:20:22.306
harvest this pathetic human's lower horn.

00:20:22.389 --> 00:20:23.974
Yeah!

00:20:24.308 --> 00:20:26.351
Wait, what am I saying?

00:20:26.435 --> 00:20:28.812
If I poach this beast's lower horn,

00:20:28.896 --> 00:20:32.482
am I any better than that ranger
with his demented foot lust?

00:20:33.317 --> 00:20:35.485
Yes, but not by enough.

00:20:37.779 --> 00:20:38.989
Score.

00:20:40.407 --> 00:20:44.620
This human's lower horn
is one of God's creatures,

00:20:44.703 --> 00:20:46.246
a living thing.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.499
And all living things, large and small...

00:20:49.583 --> 00:20:52.211
In this case, small. Whoo!

00:20:52.294 --> 00:20:56.173
...have dignity and a spark of the divine.

00:20:59.051 --> 00:21:04.097
That's the gentle, sensitive poet warlord
I fell in love with.

00:21:22.282 --> 00:21:26.286
Uh, you'll want to retreat
to a safe 500-meter radius!

00:21:28.997 --> 00:21:32.417
Well, Fry, it looks like you get
to hold on to your lower horn.

00:21:32.501 --> 00:21:35.087
As usual. Whoo!

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:36.880
Run away!

00:21:39.383 --> 00:21:40.592
Oh, yeah...

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:58.652
You're on a scenic route

00:21:58.735 --> 00:22:01.738
through a state recreation area
known as the human mind.

00:22:01.822 --> 00:22:04.199
You ask a passerby for directions,

00:22:04.283 --> 00:22:06.577
only to find he has no face, or something.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:09.162
Suddenly, up ahead, a door in the road.

00:22:09.246 --> 00:22:12.332
You swerve, narrowly avoiding
The Scary Door.

00:22:14.793 --> 00:22:18.088
I have combined the DNA
of the world's most evil animals

00:22:18.172 --> 00:22:20.424
to make the most evil creature
of them all.

00:22:24.595 --> 00:22:26.180
It turns out it's man.